          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structures on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor categories
            are models for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-categories of (∞,1)-functors
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            there are two “obvious” ways to put a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
            %em projective
            and the
            %em injective
            model structures. For completely general
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+model+category"} accessible
            (and in particular if it is
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            diagrams, additional cofibrancy-type conditions are required on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p
            A related kind of model structure is the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Reedy+model+structure"} generalized Reedy model structure
            on functor categories, which applies for
            %em any
            model category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            to be a very special sort of category, namely a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+category"} Reedy category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Reedy+category"} generalized Reedy category
          %p
            In the special case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            the projective and injective model structure on the functor categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,SSet]
            are described in more detail at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} global model structure on simplicial presheaves
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+sSet-enriched+presheaves"} model structure on sSet-enriched presheaves
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            that is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}=Set
            or else
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
            denote the enriched
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\longrightarrow C
          #ProjectiveAndInjectiveStructure.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              We define the following classes of maps in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi D
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
            %ul
              %li
                the
                %strong projective weak equivalences
                and
                %strong projective fibrations
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
                that are objectwise such morphisms in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %li
                the
                %strong injective weak equivalences
                and
                %strong injective cofibrations
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
                that are objectwise such morphisms in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              If either of these choices defines a model structure on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi D
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
              %strong projective model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]_{proj}
              or
              %strong injective model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi inj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]_{inj}
              respectively. Of course, the projective cofibrations and injective fibrations can then be characterized by lifting properties.
          %h2#existence Existence
          %h3#projective_case Projective case
          %p
            The projective model structure can be regarded as a right-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"}> transferred model structure
            \. This yields the following basic result on its existence.
          %p
          #ExistenceOfProjectiveStructureOnEnrichedFunctors.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong (existence and cofibrant generation of projective structure on enriched functors)
              %br/
              Given
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmos+for+enrichment"} cosmos for enrichment
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  ,
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  a pair of
                  = succeed "-enriched" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              carries the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              of
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
              %li
                %p
                  which admits
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copowers"} copowers
                  by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-objects"} hom-objects
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∈
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(x,y)\in \mathbf{S}
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
                %p
                  (This is the case for instance if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi S
                        %mo =
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}=
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
                  is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  is an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi S
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
                      \-model category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-objects"} hom-objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(x,y)
                  are cofibrant in
                  = succeed ".)" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            %p
              Then the projective model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]_{proj}
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
              exists, and is again cofibrantly generated.
          (For
          %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
            %semantics
              %mrow
                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                  %mi S
                %mo =
              %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S} =
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} Sets
          this is
          = succeed ".)." do
            %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn02"} Hirschhorn 2002, Thm. 11.6.1
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Assuming the existence of such copowers, for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in ob(D)
              the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation"} evaluation
              at
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ev
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ev_x \colon [D,C]\longrightarrow C
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_x
              sending
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in C
              to the functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊙
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\mapsto D(x,y)\odot A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \odot
              denotes the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} copower
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              are generating sets of cofibrations and trivial cofibrations for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^D
              be the set of maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_x(i)
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi D
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\in I
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in ob(D)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^D
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^D
              respectively, while both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^D
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi J
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^D
              permit the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              do and colimits in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
              are pointwise. Since the trivial fibrations in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
              clearly coincide with the fibrations that are weak equivalences, it remains only to show that all
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^D
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi J
                        %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊙
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(x,y)\odot j
              for maps
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\in J
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p There do exist projective model structures that do not fall under this theorem, however, such as the following.
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-trivial+model+structure"} 2-trivial model structure
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is a small 2-category, then the projective model structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
              exists.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This follows from the result of
              %a{:href => "#Lack06"} Lack
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structures"} transferred model structures
              for algebras over
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monads"} 2-monads
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
              is the category of algebras for an accessible 2-monad on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ob
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{ob(D)}
          %p
            Note that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            need not be cofibrantly generated (and the 2-trivial model structure often fails to be cofibrantly generated), so the generality of this result is not entirely included in the previous one.
          %h3#accessible_case Accessible case
          %p
            In the case when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+model+category"} accessible model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
            and its constituent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+systems"} weak factorization systems
            have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible
            realizations as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorizations"} functorial factorizations
            %a{:href => "#Moser"} Moser
            (the unenriched case appears in
            %a{:href => "#HKRS15"} HKRS15
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#GKR18"} GKR18
          %p
          #Accessible.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p Let
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
                  be a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmos"} cosmos
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  an
                  = succeed "-cocomplete" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
                  = succeed "-presentable" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
                  that is an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+model+category"} accessible model category
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
                  = succeed "-category." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            %p Then:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copowers"} copowers
                  by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-objects"} hom-objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(x,y)
                  preserve
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
                  exists and is accessible.
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copowers"} copowers
                  by the hom-objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(x,y)
                  preserve
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
                  exists and is accessible
            %p
          %h3#CombinatorialCase Combinatorial case
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
            (i.e. locally presentable and cofibrantly generated) is accessible, so Theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Accessible"}
            shows that both model structures exist, and Theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofGenProj"}
            shows that the projective model structure is cofibrantly generated, hence (by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "locally+presentable+category#PresheavesWithValuesInLocPresAreLocPres"} this Prop.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial
          %p
            In fact the injective model structure is also combinatorial, although the proof is much more involved, because there is no explicit description of the generating cofibrations and acyclic cofibrations; they have to be produced by a cardinality argument. This was first proven by in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. A.2.8.2 and A.3.3.2
            under strong assumptions on the enriching category (in particular that all objects are cofibrant), and later generalized by
            %a{:href => "#MakkaiRosický14"} Makkai &amp; Rosický 2014
            to essentially the following:
          %p
          #Combinatorial.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmos"} cosmos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              an
              = succeed "-cocomplete" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
              = succeed "-presentable" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              that is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              a small
              = succeed "-category." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copowers"} copowers
                  by the hom-objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(x,y)
                  preserve trivial cofibrations, then the projective model structure on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
                  exists and is combinatorial.
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copowers"} copowers
                  by the hom-objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(x,y)
                  preserve cofibrations, then the injective model structure on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
                  exists and is combinatorial.
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              It suffices to construct the factorizations, which follows from
              %a{:href => "#MakkaiRosický14"} Makkai &amp; Rosický 2014, Remark 3.8
              about left-lifting combinatorial weak factorization systems.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The projective and injective structures
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]_{proj}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi D
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]_{inj}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectiveAndInjectiveStructure"}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  right or left
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+categories"} proper model categories
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  is right or left proper, respectively.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+categories"} enriched model categories
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  is an
                  = succeed "-model" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{S}
          %p
            The statement about properness appears as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, remark A.2.8.4
          #PresentationOfInfinityFunctors.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]_{proj}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi inj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]_{inj}
              under the above assumptions is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(D,C^\circ)
              from the ordinary category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              to the
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-functors
            for more.
          %h3#relation_to_other_model_structures Relation to other model structures
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copowers"} copowers
              by the hom-objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              preserve trivial cofibrations, then every every fibration in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi inj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]_{inj}
              is in particular a fibration in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi D
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]_{proj}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/powers"} powers
              by the hom-objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              preserve trivial fibrations, then every cofibration in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]_{proj}
              is in particular a cofibration in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi D
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]_{inj}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is unenriched, or in the monoidal model category case if the hom-objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              are cofibrant.
          %p
            This is argued in the beginning of the proof of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, lemma A.2.8.3
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Piacenza91"} Piacenza 91, section 5
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces#ModelStructureOnTopEnrichedFunctors"} classical model structure on topological spaces – Model structure on enriched functors
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:A\longrightarrow B
              is a trivial cofibration in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in ob(D)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_x(i) : F_x(A) \longrightarrow F_x(B)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊙
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_x(A) (y) = D(x,y) \odot A
              the left adjoint of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
